        "ru-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "eb69d88b-6213-3dd9-b7ea-912c71d62f4c",
                "word": "вдругорядь",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9dad30e7-cc75-3693-b6eb-9582052b9378",
                        "entry_id": "eb69d88b-6213-3dd9-b7ea-912c71d62f4c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар., прост. в другой раз, ещё раз, снова"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a4de469-afbb-44c7-9f67-e1813c297e17",
                                "sense_id": "9dad30e7-cc75-3693-b6eb-9582052b9378",
                                "text": "Ударил все ж таки — не пожалел, а Данилушко молчит. Палач его вдругорядь — молчит, втретьи — молчит."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2905e0b-1978-4125-bdb2-d702cc5301ee",
                                "sense_id": "9dad30e7-cc75-3693-b6eb-9582052b9378",
                                "text": "Я отпустил тебе эту первую вину, а был ты, по уговору нашему, посажен за новую вину, когда ты вдругорядь на моих людей у Морозова напал."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9cf0b365-65e9-4fe0-b8e5-cf18eeef8f03",
                                "sense_id": "9dad30e7-cc75-3693-b6eb-9582052b9378",
                                "text": "Секретарь, не получавший подарков лет десять, возразил на это, что стряпчий подлец, а стряпчий отвечал, что не подлец, а тот подлец, кто платки из карманов ворует, и ударил секретаря вдругорядь в щёку."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "85f69977-9657-4d66-ad80-835ca0888556",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb69d88b-6213-3dd9-b7ea-912c71d62f4c",
                        "source_sense_id": "9dad30e7-cc75-3693-b6eb-9582052b9378",
                        "target_lang_word": "once more",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "once more",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a5c5102-3810-3ec1-a54f-8cd7a0ec1847",
                                        "entry_id": "4bcde451-dbb0-366e-a777-71fb1e07cf87",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Again, a further time, once again."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "973aeff7-eef0-4b69-a23f-b731e0e7250c",
                                                "sense_id": "8a5c5102-3810-3ec1-a54f-8cd7a0ec1847",
                                                "text": "I told him about everything I could think of; and what I couldn't think of he did. He asked about six questions during my yarn, but every question had a point to it. At the end he bowed and thanked me once more. As a thanker he was main-truck high; I never see anybody so polite."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa13bf55-daae-4686-ba5c-15b7e8332d8e",
                                                "sense_id": "8a5c5102-3810-3ec1-a54f-8cd7a0ec1847",
                                                "text": "Then everybody once more knelt, and soon the blessing was pronounced. The choir and the clergy trooped out slowly,[…], down the nave to the western door."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b95002a-ca72-4c2f-b860-c1f032effcfc",
                                                "sense_id": "8a5c5102-3810-3ec1-a54f-8cd7a0ec1847",
                                                "text": "All my best memories come back clearly to me / Some can even make me cry, just like before / It's yesterday once more"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "757f3009-f008-36f0-a2fd-7a6a030f6502",
                                        "entry_id": "4bcde451-dbb0-366e-a777-71fb1e07cf87",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see once, more."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8d18f87f-42d4-4498-ad4f-39ffdede6ba0",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb69d88b-6213-3dd9-b7ea-912c71d62f4c",
                        "source_sense_id": "9dad30e7-cc75-3693-b6eb-9582052b9378",
                        "target_lang_word": "once again",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "once again",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d45bc13-85d8-302f-834b-3b16a392d8f8",
                                        "entry_id": "3714176a-c7a8-3081-8b9a-3b671baf2707",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Again, once more, one more time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d291e05-c614-4c77-8031-7fa64039ed4c",
                                                "sense_id": "7d45bc13-85d8-302f-834b-3b16a392d8f8",
                                                "text": "In this way, President Peron terminus in Buenos Aires becomes Retiro once again, the city of Eva Peron takes its old name of La Plata, and so on."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03f53eb3-3448-43e3-937c-b5780be14559",
                                                "sense_id": "7d45bc13-85d8-302f-834b-3b16a392d8f8",
                                                "text": "Rooney's sending off will be the main talking point, however, and his actions once again raise questions about his temperament that he looked to have gone a long way towards answering in recent times."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c9fdc221-8bc6-4b24-bd91-b629cfed3fcf",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb69d88b-6213-3dd9-b7ea-912c71d62f4c",
                        "source_sense_id": "9dad30e7-cc75-3693-b6eb-9582052b9378",
                        "target_lang_word": "once over",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "once over",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3bc3c901-b8d2-3fdf-8b2d-db752b4e9c04",
                                        "entry_id": "f33106a2-268a-325e-b87d-000f09e4d15b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of once-over."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c8107ca-eb69-4d59-ae97-4f63f002431f",
                                                "sense_id": "3bc3c901-b8d2-3fdf-8b2d-db752b4e9c04",
                                                "text": "Giving your horse the once over\n Horses may seem like rather independent creatures, but in reality, they're more like half-ton toddlers. [...] That's why your horse needs what we like to call the daily once over. Every day, you must take your horse out of his stall or pasture and examine him from head to toe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6de7dbba-9203-457b-b186-370fb3279c2e",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb69d88b-6213-3dd9-b7ea-912c71d62f4c",
                        "source_sense_id": "9dad30e7-cc75-3693-b6eb-9582052b9378",
                        "target_lang_word": "abermals",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "abermals",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4fb6632-dc7a-3b6f-bf42-2c1856a3a13a",
                                        "entry_id": "be6d52e5-bfeb-3c01-a8a4-b86dcdd90fcb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "noch einmal"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d7ccbc2-637d-471b-b4f6-35ca23526199",
                                                "sense_id": "e4fb6632-dc7a-3b6f-bf42-2c1856a3a13a",
                                                "text": "Abermals fing es in den Bergen an zu regnen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e256b03-46fd-4fff-85c8-e63363d439e3",
                                                "sense_id": "e4fb6632-dc7a-3b6f-bf42-2c1856a3a13a",
                                                "text": "„Dann fiel mir der tragische Zusammenstoß bei Willdon wieder ein und all die Menschen, die jetzt Grund zur Trauer hatten, und ich war abermals den Tränen nahe.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
